    <item>
      <title>Reflection / MOP</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/reflection-or-mop/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/reflection-or-mop/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The inspiration for writing this blog post came from creation of this &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mohammadanwar_the-four-foundational-pillars-of-oop-abstraction-share-7488917976763588609-C8SQ&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LinkedIn post&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Reflection&lt;/code&gt; refers to a programming language&amp;rsquo;s capacity to analyse, alter, and execute its own code or structure during program&amp;rsquo;s execution.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There was no distinction between data and instructions in the early computers. During that period, the programs were used to analyse their memory addresses and modify the available instructions at the same time.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
